# CIDRella — minimal sudoers for the service account.
#
# As of v0.4.11, almost all sudo callsites have been replaced by polkit-gated
# systemctl calls (see /etc/polkit-1/rules.d/49-cidrella.rules). The original
# sudo-based path was broken by the v0.4.8 hardening on cidrella.service:
# directives like RestrictSUIDSGID=, ProtectKernelTunables=, etc. implicitly
# set NoNewPrivileges=yes per systemd.exec(5), which blocks setuid escalation
# and breaks every sudo call from the cidrella process. polkit + D-Bus does
# not depend on setuid, so it works under NoNewPrivileges.
#
# arping is the last remaining sudo dependency. The scanner uses
# /usr/sbin/arping for ARP-layer host discovery and arping requires raw
# sockets, which aren't reachable through any systemd unit pattern. The
# follow-up plan (PLAN.md, v0.4.12 candidate) is to either:
#   (a) setcap cap_net_raw+ep /usr/sbin/arping and call it without sudo, or
#   (b) replace arping with a Node raw-socket library and drop the binary
#       dependency entirely (the bundled Node already has cap_net_raw).
# Option (b) is preferred because it removes a binary from the trust surface.
cidrella ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/sbin/arping *
